      "math_academy_id": "q-317658",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Let $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩$ and $d=⟨4,0,-3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+0-15}{4+1+25}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-23}{30}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{23}{15},-\\frac{23}{30},-\\frac{23}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
